    "result": "## \u2705 All Tests Passing\n\n**Summary of fixes:**\n\n1. **Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`): Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`. The test file was importing these as named exports but they were only available in the default export, causing the import to fail.\n\n2. **Toxicity metric function signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`): Updated `toxicityMetric` to accept a `_references` parameter (ignored via underscore convention) as the second argument. This allows the function to be called by `runEvaluations` with both outputs and references, while correctly ignoring the references and using the default banned terms. Previously, the references array was being incorrectly treated as banned terms, causing valid outputs to be flagged as toxic.\n\n**Test results:** All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass. \u2713",
